# Written by `next dev` on every run (Next.js generates agent instruction files
# beside the app). They are machine output, they change with the Next.js
# version, and `apps/web/CLAUDE.md` would silently add rules to every agent
# session working in that directory — which is the maintainer's choice to make
# in the root CLAUDE.md, not a dev server's. Ignored, not committed; `next dev`
# recreates them locally whenever it wants them.
apps/web/AGENTS.md
apps/web/CLAUDE.md
